The reason that writes are slower than reads on HDs is that the drive has to
generate ECC information, but more importantly, the drive re-reads the data back
in to check that it was written successfully (RAW - ReadAfterWrite).  As you can
see, much optimization is done in the drive itself so that write performance isn't
half of read performance.

