>I should be using PC100 ECC SDRAM w/ EEPROM and SPD. Now what
>is a SPD and can I live without one? Comparing RAM prices
>on pricewatch.com finds 128MB of micron for $ 105 with the
>above specs. So say I don't need RAM with the SPD. Will
>having it available on the RAM affect the system operation?
>I want to be sure because returning RAM because if it's good
>but the wrong kind usually incurs a hefty restocking fee.
>
>Or someone could really make my life easier and send  me
>a quote on some Virtium ram. Of whom I can't seem to buy
>online.
Despite what you have read, you want unbuffered, NOT SPD, NOT registered.
Same RAM as works in a UP100/1100 is fine in an LX or UX board.


