At the SRM prompt:

set bootdef_dev dka0
set boot_osflags 0

You can then just type "boot" at the prompt to boot, or you can also
set:

set auto_action boot

and your machine will automatically boot into linux without waiting at
the SRM prompt.

See the manual:
http://www.redhat.com/support/manuals/RHL-7-Manual/alpha-install-guide/s1-guimode-post-installation.html

Cheers,

Matt

