		=

<SPAN class=3D"reg">The Victorian Partnership for Advanced Computing (VPA=
C) offers a unique opportunity for a person to manage their High Performa=
nce Computing (HPC) Facility.  <BR><BR>VPAC is a consortium of six univer=
sities that aims to improve the effectiveness and competitiveness of Vict=
orian universities, research institutes and industry through the provisio=
n, support and effective use of advanced computing facilities and technol=
ogies across all fields of research and industry sectors.<BR><BR>The foun=
ding members of VPAC are La Trobe University, Monash University, RMIT Uni=
versity, Swinburne University of Technology, the University of Ballarat a=
nd the University of Melbourne.  VPAC has recently been successful in rec=
eiving Victorian Government funding through the Science, Technology and I=
nnovation Initiative and is a founding partner of the Australian Partners=
hip for Advanced Computing (APAC).<BR> <BR>VPAC will be operating a 128-p=
rocessor Compaq AlphaServer SC System running True-64 UNIX that will be t=
he largest super computer installed within Australia to date.<BR><BR>Repo=
rting to the Chief Executive Officer, the System Manager's responsibiliti=
es will include<BR><BR>=B7	Managing the access to and services provided b=
y VPAC's HPC Facility<BR>=B7	Implementation of practices and procedures w=
ithin the Facility. eg. for security<BR>=B7	Develop performance measures =
and targets for activities and services<BR>=B7	Management of budget submi=
ssions for the provision of facilities and services<BR>=B7	Develop and ma=
intain relationships with Members, Vendors and Industry Users.<BR>=B7	Dev=
elop and maintain an overall strategic facilities plan <BR>=B7	Manage the=
 selection and acquisition of computer hardware and software and associat=
ed licensing.<BR><BR>You will need a relevant tertiary qualification and/=
or equivalent training and experience within this field.  An attractive r=
emuneration package will be negotiated with the successful applicant.  <B=
R><BR>Intending applicants can obtain a copy of the position description =
from www.vicpac.org.  Applications should be forwarded to the attention o=
f Karen Iatrou, Victorian Partnership for Advanced Computing, P O Box, 20=
1, Carlton South,  Vic.,  3053 or email to:  karen@vicpac.org.  <BR><BR>A=
pplications close 8th December, 2000.<BR></SPAN>
