I think I can work out the problem here. What you've got in
/usr/include/linux
and /usr/include/asm is not the same as what's in
/usr/src/linux/include/{linux,asm}.
They're probably from an earlier kernel version. I'd suggest backing
them up and then
ln -s /usr/src/linux/include/{linux,asm} /usr/include/{linux,asm}. That
should make
all the include files self-consistent.

cheers
john




