but, with this command(text mode)...(found at the manual again)

boot dkb500 -fi /kernels/vmlinux.gz -fl "root=/dev/scd0 initrd=images/ramdisk.img text"

it pass thru...

You may say that the video driver is not compatible but how come I was able to install v6.2 without any problem(GUI base).


2. Anyway, I tried to install redhat v7.0 thru text mode by default installation(web server mode), just to test our Alpha. After the smooth installation and reboots, continue to boot up until it reaches the login prompt. My problem now is, I can't log. After entering my login name or root username and press enter, it just go back to the prompt immediately without prompting you for a password. What can I do with this?

 
3. how do I single boot in Redhat Alpha?

   In linux(intel base), I only pass this paramaters... "linux single" upon prompt during the initial booting in linux. In Alpha, I supposed it would be in the SRM prompt, but how do we do this?


Many thanks again for your advance help...

noelt.


