Hm, "works for me" (TM).  On a RH 5.2 based system I have
# rpm -q sysklogd
sysklogd-1.3.31-1.6

and for 'rpm -q --changelog sysklogd' those few top entries are:

* Thu Sep 14 2000 Bill Nottingham <notting@redhat.com>

- more fixes from solar@false.com, dan@debian.org; fix the security fix

* Tue Sep 12 2000 Jakub Jelinek <jakub@redhat.com>

- never ever pass an user supplied string as 2nd arg to syslog

* Tue Nov 16 1999 Bill Nottingham <notting@redhat.com>

- fix ECONNRESETs
......

I guess that the latest one is your trouble.

