SRM, the video card I have just isn't compatible, and since I'm trying to
keep this cheap, I'm not rushing out to buy another one. So it's back to
arc and Milo.

I really do hope that Compaq fixes SRM so that it can use more than just a
few cards.  So far of the 3 cards I have available to me, SRM doesn't run
any of them (ATI, 3dFx and a creative).  They are all good cards and work
great in other machines (i386).  It's sad to see alpha's limited by what
is surely a simple fix.

I'll let you know what I find when I get ARC reinstalled.  Maybe this
puter sat to close to the british car and Lucas Gremlins have escaped from
the Triumph and infected my alpha?


